{{:media:buffalo:g300nh_a2_serial_port.png?320x240&direct|Serial port on PCB ver2 A1 A0}}

The slot surrounded by a square is  Pin 1 VCC +3.3V.

| **Pin 1**   | VCC +3.3V      |
| **Pin 2**   | GND            |
| **Pin 3**   | TX             |
| **Pin 4**   | RX             |
| Settings    | 115200,8,N,1   |

On the WZR-300HP, Pin 1 does not supply +3.3V. There is a 0 K resistor right next to pin one which can be bridged to complete the +3.3V circuit. Unfortunately, it is covered in solder now, but I believe that it was labeled R347 on the silk screen. Once this is completed, the serial console will function. If you are using a USB TTL cable, this may not be necessary.

**DO NOT CONNECT VCC**, since this will most likely irreversably damage your hardware.

