===== Two flashes of diag every few seconds =====
 * If you see the diag light flash twice about every 2-3 seconds, it means the flashing did not work properly. I did a TFTP recovery using the factory firmware ( I count exactly 10 seconds from power on before sending the TFTP File ), and it flashed. ( remember to wait 5-6 minutes after a tftp recovery ).

===== Revision A1A0 and WZR-HP-G302H A1A0 (Japanese variant) =====
WZR-HP-G302H is Japanese market name for WZR-HP-G300NH2, and seems to have slightly different WiFi chip, Atheros AR9283-AL1A. It is very probable that WZR-HP-G302H A1A0 and WZR-HP-G302H A1A0 have an identical motherboar inside, as both have dual 16MiB SPI flash chips just like WZR-HP-AG300H, with erase size of 64k. This means default WZR-HP-G300NH2 jffs2 image will not work correctly (one can fix this by modifying target/linux/ar71xx/image/Makefile, search for WZR-HP-G300NH2 profile and change fs_128k to fs_64k). WZR-HP-G302H A1A0 motherboard silk-print label says:

  WZR-HP-G302HV2
  21514W302HV21A2 Rev:A2

Similarly to Japanese variant of WZR-HP-G300NH, A1A0 comes with locked buffalo u-boot v1.08 (based on U-Boot 1.1.4 for BUFFALO AIRSTATION, PB93), see [[toh/buffalo/wzr-hp-g300h#locked_u-boot_too_short_time_tftp_window]] for details. Furthermore, this newest buffalo u-boot BS does not even provide serial console at boot time! But TFTP "blind" flash to OpenWRT was possible when accept_open_rt_fmt=1 was set (tested and confirmed ok with r31678 squashfs, try it at your own risk). Also, it is possible to circumvent serial console lock by setting force_uart variable in a similar manner to accept_open_rt_fmt.

In addition, proper fw_env.config for uboot-envtools for A1A0 variant is:
  #MTD device name        Device offset   Env. size       Flash sector size
  /dev/mtd0               0x40000         0x10000         0x10000

